# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Editors / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Node
node_modules/
dist/

# --- runtime data -----------------------------------------------------------
#
# ecoinsight.db is written by the estimation loop roughly every 1.5 seconds and
# reached 9 MB within a week. Tracking it makes every `git status` dirty, every
# pull a conflict, and every commit ~9 MB heavier. It is this machine's
# measurement history, not source.
backend/GreenIT/data/*.db
backend/GreenIT/data/*.db-journal
# WAL mode (see get_connection) keeps a write-ahead log and a shared-memory
# index alongside the database. Both are regenerated from the .db and are
# meaningless in a checkout.
backend/GreenIT/data/*.db-wal
backend/GreenIT/data/*.db-shm
backend/GreenIT/data/*.backup-*.db
# Isolated session databases from `--database ./test-user.db`. They live at the
# backend root rather than under GreenIT/data, so the rule above misses them,
# and they reached 270+ measurement rows within minutes of testing.
backend/*.db
backend/*.db-wal
backend/*.db-shm
# Rotated logs too: the bare *.log rule further down does not match
# agent.log.20260822, so a rotation left an 2.7 MB file staged for commit.
backend/GreenIT/data/agent.log*

# ...but its automatic backups are. CalibrationWriter copies hardware.db
# before every save and delete, because that file is the only record of every
# sweep anybody has run and re-measuring a model costs hours of controlled
# discharge. The copies are 20 KB each and accumulate one per edit.
backend/GreenIT/database/data/*.backup-*.db

# hardware.db is deliberately NOT ignored: it holds the per-machine
# calibration profile, it is 20 KB, and it changes only when somebody reruns a
# sweep. Losing it means recalibrating from scratch.

# DataGrip / database tooling leaves these behind.
identifier.sqlite
*.sqlite-shm
*.sqlite-wal

# Claude Code: settings.json is shared project configuration and IS tracked.
# settings.local.json is the personal override - it accumulates one-off
# permissions granted during a debugging session, including hardcoded ports
# from whatever was being tested that day, and means nothing on another
# machine.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Scratch
temp.py
*.log
